{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"37d3e2357e58f020","name":"card_event_lurking_danger","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/Allegiance/events/card_event_lurking_danger","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"LURKING DANGER","text":"Draw two random countermeasures from your deck.","flavorText":"Early in the war commanders of the Kriegsmarine believed that an effective submarine warfare strategy could bring Britain to its knees. A tactic called Rudeltaktik was implemented (also known as “wolfpack”) where submarines would spread across a projected course of a convoy and attack them “en masse” when sighted. This tactic changed how submarines were used in warfare, but prior to WWII they had been seen as lone ambushers, or as fleet attachments and to be used as destroyers. Most navy commander also thought that submarine warfare was dishonorable compared to other types of fleet engagements. Nevertheless, the Rudeltaktik proved successful early in the war and German U-boat commanders were seen as heroes in Germany, but nevertheless they failed to stop supplies from reaching the Allies and to knock Britain out of the war. Some historians believe that the German U-boat arm was close to win the Battle of the Atlantic, while others believe that they were far from it.","faction":"Germany","type":"order","rarity":"Unique","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_lurking_danger","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_lurking_danger_title","SourceString":"LURKING DANGER","LocalizedString":"LURKING DANGER"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_lurking_danger_text","SourceString":"Draw two random countermeasures from your deck.","LocalizedString":"Draw two random countermeasures from your deck."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_lurking_danger_history","SourceString":"Early in the war commanders of the Kriegsmarine believed that an effective submarine warfare strategy could bring Britain to its knees. A tactic called Rudeltaktik was implemented (also known as “wolfpack”) where submarines would spread across a projected course of a convoy and attack them “en masse” when sighted. This tactic changed how submarines were used in warfare, but prior to WWII they had been seen as lone ambushers, or as fleet attachments and to be used as destroyers. Most navy commander also thought that submarine warfare was dishonorable compared to other types of fleet engagements. Nevertheless, the Rudeltaktik proved successful early in the war and German U-boat commanders were seen as heroes in Germany, but nevertheless they failed to stop supplies from reaching the Allies and to knock Britain out of the war. Some historians believe that the German U-boat arm was close to win the Battle of the Atlantic, while others believe that they were far from it.","LocalizedString":"Early in the war commanders of the Kriegsmarine believed that an effective submarine warfare strategy could bring Britain to its knees. A tactic called Rudeltaktik was implemented (also known as “wolfpack”) where submarines would spread across a projected course of a convoy and attack them “en masse” when sighted. This tactic changed how submarines were used in warfare, but prior to WWII they had been seen as lone ambushers, or as fleet attachments and to be used as destroyers. Most navy commander also thought that submarine warfare was dishonorable compared to other types of fleet engagements. Nevertheless, the Rudeltaktik proved successful early in the war and German U-boat commanders were seen as heroes in Germany, but nevertheless they failed to stop supplies from reaching the Allies and to knock Britain out of the war. Some historians believe that the German U-boat arm was close to win the Battle of the Atlantic, while others believe that they were far from it."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Expansion2019","isReserved":true,"usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::ERegisteredCardFunction_MAX"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'AU_Order_UBoat_04'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Orders/U_Boat/AU_Order_UBoat_04.0"},"soundAttack":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'AU_Order_UBoat_04'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Orders/U_Boat/AU_Order_UBoat_04.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Germany/t_sub_wolf.t_sub_wolf","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Wikimedia Commons","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/LURKING_DANGER.LURKING_DANGER","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":1024.0,"Y":828.0},"historyPhotoSource":"Australian War Memorial ","historyPhotoIdentificationCode":"304949","historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_lurking_danger_photo","SourceString":"U-848 under attack by a US Navy Liberator, 1943.","LocalizedString":"U-848 under attack by a US Navy Liberator, 1943."},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":""}},"variables":[{"name":"possibleCards","type":"TArray<UBaseCardObject*>","direction":"in"},{"name":"pickedCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"ExecuteUbergraph_card_event_lurking_danger","owner":"card_event_lurking_danger_C","params":[{"name":"EntryPoint","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"pure":false,"event":false,"flags":"FUNC_Final | FUNC_UbergraphFunction | FUNC_HasDefaults","locals":[{"name":"Temp_int_Array_Index_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"Temp_int_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_LessEqual_IntInt_ReturnValue","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Add_IntInt_ReturnValue","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"K2Node_Event_targetCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"Temp_int_Loop_Counter_Variable","type